# e2eTest Setup and Configuration

## Installing `nvm`

If you don't have `nvm` installed yet, you can download and install it by following the instructions from the official repository:

- [Install NVM](https://github.com/nvm-sh/nvm#installing-and-updating)

## Updating NPM Dependencies

To update the npm dependencies locally on your machine, follow these steps:

1. Install Node.js version `22.0.0` using `nvm`:
    ```bash
    nvm install 22.0.0
    ```

2. Use the installed Node.js version:
    ```bash
    nvm use 22.0.0
    ```

3. Update the `package-lock.json`:
    ```bash
    npm install --package-lock-only
    ```

4. Commit the changes made to `package-lock.json`.

Ensure that `nvm` is installed and properly configured on your machine to set
up a fully functional Node.js/npm environment.

## Overrides and known advisories

`package.json` carries an `overrides` block: `eth-cli` 2.0.2 (the last release,
unmaintained) pins `web3@1.2.1` and drags in old transitive dependencies, so the
advisories reported by `npm audit` (and by the `npm_audit` CI job, see
`scripts/ci/npm_audit.sh`) can only be fixed by forcing patched versions. Keep
the overrides within the major version the dependent expects, and after any
change run the Etherlink tezt suite (`etherlink.daily` pipeline) on the rebuilt
image: `etherlink/tezt/lib/eth_cli.ml` drives `eth-cli` (`abi:*`, `block:*`,
`address:balance`, `transaction:*`, `contract:*`).

Advisories that cannot be fixed with `eth-cli` 2.0.2 (as of November 2026):

- `elliptic` (low): no fixed release exists.
- `request` (moderate, SSRF): unmaintained, no fixed release; it is only reached
  through `web3-bzz` -> `swarm-js` -> `eth-lib` 0.1 -> `servify` and is never
  loaded by the `eth-cli` commands used in the tests.
- `decode-uri-component` (high since GHSA-qr28-fpjm-wq7f, which affects every
  release up to 0.5.0): the only fixed release, 0.5.1, is ESM-only and breaks
  the CommonJS `query-string` -> `xhr-request` chain used by `web3`'s HTTP
  provider. `query-string`, `xhr-request` and `xhr-request-promise` are
  reported as high for that reason alone.
- `web3` 1.2.1 and its `web3-core-*` packages (moderate: prototype pollution,
  credential storage in the browser wallet): overriding the `web3` family to
  1.10.4 fixes them, but web3 1.10 encodes ABI arguments with the strict
  ethers v5 coder, which rejects a negative value for a `uint` argument, and
  the Etherlink test "Check L2 contract call" relies on `set(-1)` being encoded
  as `uint256` max. Switch the test to the explicit value before bumping.

Everything else reported is a dependency of one of these. Fixing them for good
means replacing `eth-cli` (for example with `cast` from Foundry, already in the
image) in `etherlink/tezt/lib/eth_cli.ml`.

## Notes on NPM and Alpine

- To use a newer version of Node.js (v22), add `npm` from the `3.21` repository
  instead of `3.20`. This will resolve related hanging issues. For more
  details, see:
  - [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/4028)
  - [Alpine GitLab Merge
    Request](https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/merge_requests/75639)

## Datadog Integration

We use the `datadog-ci` tool to send relevant job info (e.g. pipeline type) as well as JUnit test results to Datadog during CI
jobs. Refer to the script at `[scripts/ci/tezt.sh]` for details.

### Important Notes:
- The `datadog-ci` version should be kept in sync with the version used by the
  `datadog/ci` image in the `[datadog_ci]` image (see `ci/bin/common.ml` for
  version sync details).

## Additional Dependencies

- **Ethereum (eth)**: Required for running end-to-end (e2e) tests.
- **Solidity Compiler (solc)**: Required for compiling Solidity smart contracts.
